# Project Context — Bus-Applications

Linux userspace C++17 dashboard on Raspberry Pi. Not bare-metal firmware and
not an RTOS: a single-threaded polling loop talking to `/dev/i2c-*`,
`/dev/spidev*`, and GPIO via libgpiod. Deep-dive checklists that assume
ISR/task boundaries, watchdogs, or tickless idle apply only where this
userspace process actually shares state or hardware — flag those as
not-applicable rather than blocking, unless a change introduces real
concurrency.

- **coding_standard:** none — use skill defaults. Language is C++17;
  errors on bus I/O are reported via exceptions (`std::runtime_error` /
  `std::invalid_argument`). Keep bus wrappers (`I2CDevice`, `SPIDevice`)
  free of device protocol; keep device drivers free of dashboard/UI logic.
- **architecture_reference:** `docs/architecture.md`
- **criticality:** non-critical (lab / learning dashboard; may downgrade
  non-safety fault-posture findings to advisory per skill Decision Rules)
- **known_deviations:**
  - Single-threaded polling in `src/app.cpp`; no mutex/arbiter on I2C or
    SPI. Each I2C driver opens its own `/dev/i2c-1` file descriptor.
    Acceptable while there is one caller; a second thread or process on
    the same bus is out of scope.
  - LCD1602 bit-bangs HD44780 over GPIO with busy-wait microsecond delays
    (`delay_us`). That is required by the controller timing, not a missed
    low-power wait.
  - No HIL suite in CI yet. `scripts/hil_test.sh` on the Pi covers automated
    smoke (I2C scan, app run); operator steps document pot, LED bar, and LCD.
  - Unit tests: `ads7830_protocol_test`, `hc595_bar_test` via `ctest` on host/Pi.
  - Main loop retries transient sensor errors (50 ms backoff) instead of exiting;
    ADS7830 `readAnalog` retries up to 3 times (10 ms between attempts).
  - Startup banner prints ADS7830 address/channel; warns if pot unchanged 5 s.
  - `I2CDevice::readRawByte()` returns the raw `i2c_smbus_read_byte`
    result (including negative errno-style failures). Callers must check;
    `ADS7830::readAnalog` does, other callers must not assume success.
  - Review reports are written under `reviews/` but are gitignored and
    must not be committed or pushed. The skill's "commit alongside the
    code" logging convention does not apply in this repo.

Update this file when the repo's standards change, or when a new deviation
is approved. Do not let this file silently go stale — a wrong default here
silently affects every review's severity judgments.
